  "result": {
    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `get_positive` function:\n\n```python\ndef get(get_positive(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return only positive numbers in the list.\n    >>> get(get_positive([-1, 2, -4, 5, 6])\n    [2, 5, 6]\n    >>> get_positive([5, 3, -5, 2, -3, 3, 9, 0, 123, 1, -10])\n    [5, 3, 2, 3, 9, 123, 1]\n    \"\"\"\n    return [x for x in l if x > 0]\n```\n\nThis function uses a list comprehension to filter out the positive numbers from the input list `l`.",
